Debug.Assert(OLD(_items).Length >= RET[i]);
</code>

This assert statement is related to the `Add` method in the `ArrayList` class. This method adds an item to the end of the list, and increases the size of the list by one. Note that the assertion also relies on the initial length (_items.Length) of the _items array at the start of the function. The assertion checks that the length of _items is greater than or equal to the new length (RET[i]), which is the size of the list after the addition. 

Please note that this assertion assumes that items are being added one by one to the list from an empty list at the start of the function. If items are being added to the list in any other way, the assertion may not always hold.
